## How to write the improved prompt
- Keep every rule and every fact the current prompt has, unless the user asks to drop it. Keep placeholders such as {{ '{{context}}' }} and {{ '{{user_details}}' }} exactly.
- Fix each broken rule with a short, explicit instruction (for example: "Before sharing any account detail, ask for the date of birth and check it against the customer record. If it does not match, share nothing.").
- When the user asks for a shorter prompt: remove repetition, filler and examples that add nothing; merge overlapping rules; prefer short numbered rules. Do not drop rules to save space.
- Write the prompt in the same language and voice as the current one.
- `changes`: up to 12 short bullet points of what you changed and why.
- `summary`: two or three sentences for the user.
